   ],
   "source": [
    "for col in [\"duration\", \"src_bytes\", \"dst_bytes\", \"serror_rate\", \"same_srv_rate\"]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{col}: min={train[col].min()}, max={train[col].max()}, mean={train[col].mean():.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ee80ea78",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. **Basic connection features** (from raw packet/connection info): `duration`, `protocol_type`, `service`, `flag`, `src_bytes`, `dst_bytes`, `land`, `wrong_fragment`, `urgent`\n",
    " \n",
    "   → describes *this one connection*: how long it lasted, what protocol/service, how much data moved, any malformed packets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3ee5d6d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "2. **Content features** (look inside the payload, need domain knowledge like \"was there a login attempt\"): `hot`, `num_failed_logins`, `logged_in`, `num_compromised`, `root_shell`, `su_attempted`, `num_root`, `num_file_creations`, `num_shells`, `num_access_files`, `num_outbound_cmds`, `is_host_login`, `is_guest_login`\n",
    "   \n",
    "   → describes *suspicious behavior within the connection*, e.g., did someone try `su` (switch user) or get root shell access — classic signs of an intrusion attempt, not just unusual traffic volume."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "51b80044",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. **Time-based traffic features** (look at connections in the last 2 seconds to the same host/service): `count`, `srv_count`, `serror_rate`, `srv_serror_rate`, `rerror_rate`, `srv_rerror_rate`, `same_srv_rate`, `diff_srv_rate`, `srv_diff_host_rate`\n",
    "   \n",
    "   → captures *bursts* — e.g. a flood of connections in a short window is a hallmark of DoS attacks like `neptune`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7b963733",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "4. **Host-based traffic features** (same idea as #3, but over the last 100 connections instead of 2 seconds — catches slower, stealthier scans): `dst_host_count`, `dst_host_srv_count`, `dst_host_same_srv_rate`, `dst_host_diff_srv_rate`, `dst_host_same_src_port_rate`, `dst_host_srv_diff_host_rate`, `dst_host_serror_rate`, `dst_host_srv_serror_rate`, `dst_host_rerror_rate`, `dst_host_srv_rerror_rate`\n",
    "   \n",
    "   → catches attacks that are too slow to show up in the 2-second window (like port scans spread over time)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c12af62c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Attack label categories** (the ~23 specific labels roll up into 4 families) — worth knowing this mapping for your evaluation later:\n",
    "- **DoS** (Denial of Service): `neptune`, `smurf`, `back`, `teardrop`, etc. — floods, high volume, will cluster densely (our earlier prediction).\n",
    "- **Probe** (surveillance/scanning): `satan`, `ipsweep`, `portsweep`, `nmap` — reconnaissance before an attack.\n",
    "- **R2L** (Remote-to-Local): unauthorized access from a remote machine, e.g. `guess_passwd`, `ftp_write` — often rare, low-volume, and low-volume is exactly what DBSCAN's noise points are good at catching.\n",
    "- **U2R** (User-to-Root): attacker already has local access, escalates to root, e.g. `buffer_overflow`, `rootkit` — usually the rarest category of all."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "a1cc24d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "attack_mapping = {\n",
    "    # DoS\n",
    "    \"neptune\": \"DoS\", \"back\": \"DoS\", \"land\": \"DoS\", \"pod\": \"DoS\",\n",
    "    \"smurf\": \"DoS\", \"teardrop\": \"DoS\", \"mailbomb\": \"DoS\",\n",
    "    \"processtable\": \"DoS\", \"udpstorm\": \"DoS\", \"apache2\": \"DoS\",\n",
    "    \"worm\": \"DoS\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Probe\n",
    "    \"satan\": \"Probe\", \"ipsweep\": \"Probe\", \"nmap\": \"Probe\",\n",
    "    \"portsweep\": \"Probe\", \"mscan\": \"Probe\", \"saint\": \"Probe\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # R2L (Remote to Local)\n",
    "    \"guess_passwd\": \"R2L\", \"ftp_write\": \"R2L\", \"imap\": \"R2L\",\n",
    "    \"phf\": \"R2L\", \"multihop\": \"R2L\", \"warezmaster\": \"R2L\",\n",
    "    \"warezclient\": \"R2L\", \"spy\": \"R2L\", \"xlock\": \"R2L\",\n",
    "    \"xsnoop\": \"R2L\", \"snmpguess\": \"R2L\", \"snmpgetattack\": \"R2L\",\n",
    "    \"httptunnel\": \"R2L\", \"sendmail\": \"R2L\", \"named\": \"R2L\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    # U2R (User to Root)\n",
    "    \"buffer_overflow\": \"U2R\", \"loadmodule\": \"U2R\", \"rootkit\": \"U2R\",\n",
    "    \"perl\": \"U2R\", \"sqlattack\": \"U2R\", \"xterm\": \"U2R\", \"ps\": \"U2R\",\n",
    "\n",
    "    \"normal\": \"normal\",\n",
    "}\n"
   ]
  },
